Section 4. PUNISHMENTS

Article 98. Punishments imposed upon juvenile offenders

A juvenile offender shall face one of the following punishments for each criminal offence committed:
1.	Warning;

2.	Fine;
3.	Community sentence;
4.	Imprisonment.

